{"findings":[{"finding":"REQ-21 lists ASM-18 as a source, which keeps gap-affected stock On Hold until resolved, but the same requirement (per Q-11/ASM-2) says the screen must not infer On Hold from a gap; the sources contradict each other and nothing settles which wins.","reqId":"REQ-21","rubric":1,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"REQ-24 and REQ-3 cite ASM-1 and ASM-17 ('No; online only'), yet REQ-24 queues offline driver actions and later syncs them under Q-10, so the sources state opposite rules for queued actions.","reqId":"REQ-24","rubric":1,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"AC-6.1 and AC-6.3 show API-recalculated 'decision values' after a profile change, but no criterion requires that a changed not-permitted-range disposition goes back through the Quality Officer proposal and different-Quality-Manager approval required by Q-1/REQ-9.","reqId":"REQ-6","rubric":1,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"Staff sign-in through 'Meridian Microsoft accounts' and a customer one-time-code step are not in any intent span or human answer (ASM-23's answer only states email, password and a reset link), so the identity provider and the second factor are unanchored.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":5,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-2.1 names the 'Meridian Microsoft' sign-in option directly instead of treating the staff identity provider or tenant as configuration.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":8,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-2.2 covers only the code-entry screen and has no criterion for a wrong, expired or repeatedly failed one-time code, or for a resend.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-14.3 says the screen 'shows only returned eligible dates' and also that it 'applies the next-working-day rule' for before and after cut-off, so it is unclear whether the browser computes eligibility or only displays what the API returns.","reqId":"REQ-14","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"'The workday ends' triggers clearing of cached route and recipient data in REQ-24, AC-24.7 and AC-24.8, but nothing defines when a workday ends or in which time zone (driver device or serving warehouse per ASM-6).","reqId":"REQ-24","rubric":6,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"In AC-24.4 the action is shown 'as rejected or no longer queued', and the EARS says queued actions are 'erased or marked rejected', so the expected end state has two acceptable outcomes and cannot be checked deterministically.","reqId":"REQ-24","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-9.4 accepts either 'shows the returned error message or disables the approval control', so a test cannot tell which behaviour is required when the proposer tries to approve their own disposition.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"No criterion covers empty states (no temperature readings, no stock rows, a filter with no matches, no alerts), even though lists and histories appear throughout REQ-3, REQ-10, REQ-19, REQ-20 and REQ-27.","reqId":"REQ-19","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Several write flows have only a success criterion, with no API-refusal or network-failure path: stock movement (AC-12.1), address changes (AC-13.1), box sealing (AC-17.3) and route creation (AC-18.1).","reqId":"REQ-12","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-10.1 asserts that the returned status quantities sum to on-hand but does not say what the screen shows if the API returns figures that do not reconcile.","reqId":"REQ-10","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-15.6 lets a Dispatcher cancel a Packed-or-later order, but no criterion says what the screen shows for the already packed box, its logger, or its place on a route after the cancellation.","reqId":"REQ-15","rubric":6,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-26.6 allows a recall to be closed without saying whether closing is allowed, blocked or warned while AC-26.4's unreconciled quantities are still outstanding.","reqId":"REQ-26","rubric":6,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-5.5 deactivates a product without covering what open orders, allocations or profile versions referencing it show afterwards, and the 'today' in AC-5.6 has no defined time zone.","reqId":"REQ-5","rubric":6,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"I-7 asks for role and warehouse access controls, but no requirement gives System Administrators a screen to assign staff roles or warehouses, or to disable accounts; only Customer Administrator invite and remove exists (REQ-4).","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-3.2 grants Quality Managers and Auditors all-warehouse views, but this scope is not anchored in any intent span or human answer.","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":5,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-3.3 requires an 'API-refused write' to be shown as an error on Auditor pages that, by the same criterion, have no create, edit or delete controls, so that error path cannot be reached through the UI.","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"To reconcile ASM-9 with ASM-21, REQ-8 adds a separate 'receipt-evidence' image/PDF upload that no intent span or answer asks for.","reqId":"REQ-8","rubric":4,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-8.1 relies on a 'configured supplier interface format' whose documentation, per ASM-8, Meridian has not yet provided, so no client-side validation of the logger file can be specified or tested.","reqId":"REQ-8","rubric":5,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"REQ-22 repeats REQ-21's gap behaviour (status and budget shown without an estimated tier charge), and its stability is 0.33, so the two requirements overlap and could drift apart.","reqId":"REQ-22","rubric":1,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"NFR-4 states volumes (1,000 users, 100,000 records, 5,000 devices) but sets no observable web-side target such as list or chart load time or pagination behaviour at that volume.","reqId":"NFR-4","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-27.1 says the CSV contains 'the displayed or filtered records', which leaves open whether it holds the current page or the full filtered set, and no criterion covers which roles may export records containing recipient names.","reqId":"REQ-27","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"REQ-15 cites Q-6 (addresses and shelf life) as a source for the order change and cancellation rules, and REQ-26 cites Q-1 for recalls; neither source supports the requirement it is attached to.","reqId":"REQ-15","rubric":5,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"No criterion covers the default language, whether the language choice persists across sessions, or how left-to-right identifiers such as lot codes and numbers render inside right-to-left Arabic pages.","reqId":"REQ-28","rubric":2,"severity":"low"}]}